Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Registration Mark in the Bass
- Story & Context: During a rehearsal, Eun-sol notices that one narrow strip of blue registration tape on the floor marks the exact place where the lowest surdo suddenly becomes fuller. Rafael moves the drum thirty centimeters to either side and the effect disappears. Hae-rin places the ajaeng at the same point and sustains a low note while Min builds a chord from the partials that bloom in the room.

The track begins with a single surdo pulse every two beats and one long ajaeng bow. Caixa enters only after the first full spectral chord appears. Lila slowly opens a resonant low-pass filter tuned near the ajaeng’s third partial, making the synth feel less like an added instrument and more like the room becoming audible.

The middle section develops into a heavy samba-reggae procession with repinique calls answered by short ajaeng slides. The climax arrives when the entire ensemble plays around the same registration mark, then suddenly cuts to one dry bow stroke and one footstep.
