Track 3: The Bow Leaves Red Dust
- Story & Context: After a long recording session, Hae-rin notices fine reddish bow residue on the edge of the ajaeng bridge. Instead of cleaning it immediately, Eun-sol places a macro microphone nearby and records the tiny scraping texture produced when the bow passes across the strings at very low pressure.

Lila filters white noise until it resembles the same granular texture, then fades between the acoustic and synthetic versions without revealing the transition point. Rafael reduces the samba-reggae groove to rim clicks, soft surdo strokes, and one delayed repinique call every eight bars. Min plays isolated Rhodes intervals based on the brightest partials in the bow noise rather than the written note.

The track’s climax is intentionally quiet. The ajaeng sustains a low tone while the granular bow residue sound spreads across the stereo field and the ensemble gradually removes all pitched accompaniment. The final sound is the bow being lifted from the string.
